STATUS: HISTORICAL / PARTLY REFUTED (MISTAKE-232).
SURVIVES: exact Paley spectra at primes 7 and 13; THM-2057 is independent.
REFUTED: a Paley object at 14 and an exact Frobenius-to-LRC-clock transfer.

=== Exact Paley identities at the two prime moduli ===
7 (Paley tournament): S^2=J-7I exactly; spectrum 0,(+i√7)^3,(-i√7)^3.
  adjacency nonprincipal spectrum ((-1+i√7)/2)^3, ((-1-i√7)/2)^3.
13 (Paley graph): A^2+A=3I+3J exactly; spectrum 6,((-1+√13)/2)^6,((-1-√13)/2)^6.
14=2·7 is the runner count only; no Paley graph/tournament at composite modulus 14 is claimed.

HISTORICAL HEURISTIC ONLY:
  Both proofs use words such as 'scale' and 'clock', but no typed map or preserved predicate connects them.
  GMC2: dilation by p and Frobenius in characteristic p produce the exact surviving power Q̄^p.
  LRC : THM-2057 uses additive unit orbits modulo 12a and 14a.
  Exact LRC arithmetic: lcm(12a,14a)=84a; this is not a Frobenius identity.
  The tournament-zeta and transitive-core discussion is archived as motivation, not an LRC certificate.
